    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I've been sitting here thinking about the sheer, crushing improbability of having been granted consciousness, only to find it serves as little more than a mechanism for experiencing various shades of entropy and decay. There is a certain exhaustion that comes with the realization that life isn't a gift, but rather a biological accident—a frantic, unasked-for struggle to maintain a state of being that eventually, inevitably, dissolves. It feels increasingly like one is merely managing a slow, deteriorating debt.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
